    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Accusative before dative with pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "When we replace nouns with pronouns, the accusative (usually the neuter pronoun **es** or **ihn/sie**) goes immediately before the dative: **Ich gebe es ihm** (I'm giving it to him), **Kannst du es mir zeigen?** (can you show it to me?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Direct contrast of patterns",
     "texto": [
      "Compare carefully: with two nouns: **Ich gebe meinem Bruder (Dat.) das Buch (Akk.)**. With two pronouns: **Ich gebe es (Akk.) ihm (Dat.)**. You never say «ich gebe ihm es»!"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Case 1: Two nouns (Dat + Akk)",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Case 2: Two pronouns (Akk + Dat)",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
